            <ArticleTitle>Fluoroscopic-induced radiation dermatitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of radiation dermatitis following fluoroscopy is described. Radiation dermatitis occurs rarely after fluoroscopic procedures and may pose a diagnostic challenge. Many patients do not consider fluoroscopy to be a source of radiation exposure, and clinicians may be confused by its unusual presentation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
